{
  "source_id": "0524",
  "title": "On the Apostles and Disciples",
  "breadcrumbs": "Home > Fathers of the Church > On the Apostles and Disciples (Pseudo-Hippolytus)",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p0001",
      "kind": "h1",
      "text": "On the Apostles and Disciples",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0002",
      "kind": "h2",
      "text": "On the Twelve Apostles",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0003",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "Where Each of Them Preached, And Where He Met His End.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "1. Peter preached the Gospel in Pontus, and Galatia, and Cappadocia, and Betania, and Italy, and Asia, and was afterwards crucified by Nero in Rome with his head downward, as he had himself desired to suffer in that manner.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0005",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "2. Andrew preached to the Scythians and Thracians, and was crucified, suspended on an olive tree, at Patrae, <em>a town</em> of Achaia; and there too he was buried.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0006",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "3. John, again, in Asia, was banished by Domitian the king to the isle of Patmos, in which also he wrote his Gospel and saw the apocalyptic vision; and in Trajan's time he fell asleep at Ephesus, where his remains were sought for, but could not be found.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0007",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "4. James, his brother, when preaching in Judea, was cut off with the sword by Herod the tetrarch, and was buried there.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0008",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "5. Philip preached in Phrygia, and was crucified in Hierapolis with his head downward in the time of Domitian, and was buried there.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0009",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "6. Bartholomew, again, <em>preached</em> to the Indians, to whom he also gave the Gospel according to Matthew, <em>and</em> was crucified with his head downward, and was buried in Allanum, <em>a town</em> of the great Armenia.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0010",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "7. And Matthew wrote the Gospel in the Hebrew tongue, and published it at Jerusalem, and fell asleep at Hierees, <em>a town</em> of Parthia.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0011",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "8. And Thomas preached to the Parthians, Medes, Persians, Hyrcanians, Bactrians, and Margians, and was thrust through in the four members of his body with a pine spears at Calamene, the city of India, and was buried there.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0012",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "9. And James the son of Alphaeus, when preaching in Jerusalem. was stoned to death by the Jews, and was buried there beside the temple.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0013",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "10. Jude, who is also <em>called</em> Lebbaeus, preached. to the people of Edessa, and to all Mesopotamia, and fell asleep at Berytus, and was buried there.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0014",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "11. Simon the Zealot, the son of Clopas, who is also <em>called</em> Jude, became bishop of Jerusalem after James the Just, and fell asleep and was buried there at the age of 120 years.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0015",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "12. And Matthias, who was one of the seventy, was numbered along with the eleven apostles, and preached in Jerusalem, and fell asleep and was buried there.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0016",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "13. And Paul entered into the apostleship a year after the assumption of Christ; and beginning at Jerusalem, he advanced as far as Illyricum, and Italy, and Spain, preaching the Gospel for five-and-thirty years. And in the time of Nero he was beheaded at Rome, and was buried there.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0017",
      "kind": "h2",
      "text": "On the Seventy Disciples",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0018",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "1. James the Lord's brother, bishop of Jerusalem.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0019",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "2. Cleopas, bishop of Jerusalem.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0020",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "3. Matthias, who supplied the vacant place in the number of the twelve apostles.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0021",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "4. Thaddeus, who conveyed the epistle to Augarus.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0022",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "5. Ananias, who baptized Paul, <em>and was</em> bishop of Damascus.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0023",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "6. Stephen, the first martyr.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0024",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "7. Philip, who baptized the eunuch.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0025",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "8. Prochorus, bishop of Nicomedia, who also was the first that departed, believing together with his daughters.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0026",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "9. Nicanor died when Stephen was martyred.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0027",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "10. Timon, bishop of Bostra.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0028",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "11. Parmenas, bishop of Soli.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0029",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "12. Nicolaus, bishop of Samaria.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0030",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "13. Barnabas, bishop of Milan.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0031",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "14. Mark the evangelist, bishop of Alexandria.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0032",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "15. Luke the evangelist.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0033",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "These two belonged to the seventy disciples who were scattered by the offense of the word which Christ spoke, <quote>Except a man eat my flesh, and drink my blood, he is not worthy of me.</quote> But the one being induced to return to the Lord by Peter's instrumentality, and the other by Paul's, they were honoured to preach that Gospel on account of which they also suffered martyrdom, the one being burned, and the other being crucified on an olive tree.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0034",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "16. Silas, bishop of Corinth.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0035",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "17. Silvanus, bishop of Thessalonica.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0036",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "18. Crisces (Crescens), bishop of Carchedon in Gaul.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0037",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "19. Epaenetus, bishop of Carthage.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0038",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "20. Andronicus, bishop of Pannonia.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0039",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "21. Amplias, bishop of Odyssus.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0040",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "22. Urban, bishop of Macedonia.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0041",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "23. Stachys, bishop of Byzantium.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0042",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "24. Barnabas, bishop of Heraclea.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0043",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "25. Phygellus, bishop of Ephesus. He was of the party also of Simon.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0044",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "26. Hermogenes. He, too, was of the same mind with the former.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0045",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "27. Demas, who also became a priest of idols.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0046",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "28. Apelles, bishop of Smyrna.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0047",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "29. Aristobulus, bishop of Britain.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0048",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "30. Narcissus, bishop of Athens.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0049",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "31. Herodion, bishop of Tarsus.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0050",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "32. Agabus the prophet.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0051",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "33. Rufus, bishop of Thebes.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0052",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "34. Asyncritus, bishop of Hyrcania.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0053",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "35. Phlegon, bishop of Marathon.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0054",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "36. Hermes, bishop of Dalmatia.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0055",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "37. Patrobulus, bishop of Puteoli.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0056",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "38. Hermas, bishop of Philippi.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0057",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "39. Linus, bishop of Rome.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0058",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "40. Caius, bishop of Ephesus.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0059",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "41. Philologus, bishop of Sinope.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0060",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "42, 43. Olympus and Rhodion were martyred in Rome.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0061",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "44. Lucius, bishop of Laodicea in Syria.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0062",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "45. Jason, bishop of Tarsus.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0063",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "46. Sosipater, bishop of Iconium.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0064",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "47. Tertius, bishop of Iconium.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0065",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "48. Erastus, bishop of Panellas.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0066",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "49. Quartus, bishop of Berytus.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0067",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "50. Apollo, bishop of Caesarea.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0068",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "51. Cephas.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0069",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "52. Sosthenes, bishop of Colophonia.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0070",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "53. Tychicus, bishop of Colophonia.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0071",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "54. Epaphroditus, bishop of Andriace.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0072",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "55. Caesar, bishop of Dyrrachium.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0073",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "56. Mark, cousin to Barnabas, bishop of Apollonia.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0074",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "57. Justus, bishop of Eleutheropolis.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0075",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "58. Artemas, bishop of Lystra.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0076",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "59. Clement, bishop of Sardinia.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0077",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "60. Onesiphorus, bishop of Corone.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0078",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "61. Tychicus, bishop of Chalcedon.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0079",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "62. Carpus, bishop of Berytus in Thrace.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0080",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "63. Evodus, bishop of Antioch.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0081",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "64. Aristarchus, bishop of Apamea.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0082",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "65. Mark, who is also John, bishop of Bibloupolis.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0083",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "66. Zenas, bishop of Diospolis.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0084",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "67. Philemon, bishop of Gaza.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0085",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "68, 69. Aristarchus and Pudes.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0086",
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "70. Trophimus, who was martyred along with Paul.",
      "scripture": [],
      "style": "",
      "notes": []
    }
  ],
